[s0l0!-header][h1]Calling Methods [/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

You can call a method as many times as necessary. 
When a method runs, the code jumps down to where the method is defined, executes the code inside of it, then goes back and proceeds to the next line.
[s0l0!-header][b]Example:[/b][/s0l0!-header] [code format="java" codeId="753"]class MyClass {
  
  static void sayHello() {
    System.out.println("Hello World!");
  }

  public static void main(String[ ] args) {
    sayHello();
    sayHello();
    sayHello();
  }
}
[/code]
[note]In cases like the one above, where the same thing is repeated over and over, you can achieve the same result using loops (while or for).[/note]
